Usage: /etc/profiles/per-user/tom/bin/home-manager [OPTION] COMMAND

Options

  -f FILE           The home configuration file.
                    Default is '~/.config/nixpkgs/home.nix'.
  -A ATTRIBUTE      Optional attribute that selects a configuration
                    expression in the configuration file.
  -I PATH           Add a path to the Nix expression search path.
  --flake flake-uri Use Home Manager configuration at flake-uri
                    Default is '~/.config/home-manager'.
  -b EXT            Move existing files to new path rather than fail.
  -v                Verbose output
  -n                Do a dry run, only prints what actions would be taken
  -h                Print this help
  --version         Print the Home Manager version

Options passed on to nix-build(1)

  --arg(str) NAME VALUE    Override inputs passed to home-manager.nix
  --cores NUM
  --debug
  --impure
  --keep-failed
  --keep-going
  -j, --max-jobs NUM
  --option NAME VALUE
  -L, --print-build-logs
  --log-format FORMAT
  --show-trace
  --(no-)substitute
  --no-out-link            Do not create a symlink to the output path
  --no-write-lock-file
  --builders VALUE
  --refresh                Consider all previously downloaded files out-of-date

Commands

  help         Print this help

  edit         Open the home configuration in $VISUAL or $EDITOR

  option OPTION.NAME
               Inspect configuration option named OPTION.NAME.

  build        Build configuration into result directory

  init [--switch] [DIR]
      Initializes a configuration in the given directory. If the directory
      does not exist, then it will be created. The default directory is
      '~/.config/home-manager'.

      --switch      Immediately activate the generated configuration.

  instantiate  Instantiate the configuration and print the resulting derivation

  switch [OPTION]
      Build and activate configuration

      --rollback    Do not build a new configuration, instead roll back to
                    the configuration prior to the current configuration.

      -c, --specialisation NAME
                    Activates the named specialisation; when not specified,
                    switching will activate the unspecialised configuration.

  generations  List all home environment generations

  remove-generations ID...
      Remove indicated generations. Use 'generations' command to
      find suitable generation numbers.

  repl
      Opens the configuration in `nix repl`

  expire-generations TIMESTAMP
      Remove generations older than TIMESTAMP where TIMESTAMP is
      interpreted as in the -d argument of the date tool. For
      example "-30 days" or "2018-01-01".

  packages     List all packages installed in home-manager-path

  news         Show news entries in a pager

  uninstall    Remove Home Manager
